  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Platform for Humanitarian Knowledge Exchange - KUNO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KUNO (Kennis Uitwisseling over Noodhulp - Dutch for: Humanitarian Knowledge Exchange) brings together available humanitarian knowledge in the Netherlands from practitioners, academics and policy-makers, and connects the Dutch humanitarian field to knowledge outside the Netherlands and outside the humanitarian sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target groups already reflected in the members and donors of KUNO are: Practitioners from NGOs; Academics from universities or knowledge institutes; Policy makers from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Other target groups, not (yet) reflected in the membership or the donors, but also relevant for the knowledge platform, are corporate and private actors, and the diaspora representatives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of KUNO is to strengthen humanitarian action and Dutch humanitarian thought leadership by stimulating learning, reflection and debate. In this way, KUNO contributes to new policy, new practices, and new research that will result in more efficient and effective humanitarian practices.</narrative>
  </description>
